From 7bf3eb65b1d2b9cf56c28db81439286d9f43d4c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX Project <micronux@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] riscv: add ESP32-P4 NOMMU platform support

The ESP32-P4 HP core only implements CLIC mode.  Its mtvec base is
64-byte aligned, its interrupt enables are memory mapped, and its mcause
register carries CLIC state in addition to the architectural cause code.

Add the minimum platform support needed by MicroNUX: revision-1.3 CLIC
handling, CLINT timer enable, polling USB Serial/JTAG early console,
ROM-assisted restart, and the 0x48400000 NOMMU link address used by the
loader contract.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX Project <micronux@example.invalid>
